invariant: INV-38
file: src/srv_out.c
catches: webpki_loop_tx_record
reason: a tcp-nonblocking server cuts its protected handshake records at
  CH_TX_PT, as a blocking build does, while its ch_tls.tx holds the hello
  alone (session.h), so in a TX_RECORD build a message longer than that
  array does not fit one record and the handshake fails with
  internal_error. The TX_RECORD loop seals one such message.

--- old
    return t->peer_limit < CH_TX_HANDSHAKE_PT ? t->peer_limit : CH_TX_HANDSHAKE_PT;
--- new
    return t->peer_limit < CH_TX_PT ? t->peer_limit : CH_TX_PT;
